# Pavilion vs SHMS deploys

Build **Pavilion** as if SHMS never existed (product, tenants, `onpavilion.com`, demo/trials). No Stone Hill PII or school cost on Pavilion.

Stone Hill (`frontend` / www.shmspto.org) and Pavilion apps (`commons-pto-demo`, `commons-pto`, `commons-site`) share this monorepo for now but are **separate products**.

Application ships follow **Staging-first** in `ship-after-serena.mdc` and **`shms-deploy-git.mdc`** (critical, every agent):

1. Serena QA → commit in **`auraflux-dev/shmspto`** for Stone Hill (port `frontend/` diffs from this monorepo if needed).
2. **Staging review** on **https://shmspto.vercel.app** when staging is current (visitor-facing). Never use ephemeral Preview URLs for Rob review.
3. **STOP.** Wait for explicit OK on visitor changes.
4. **`git push origin main`** on **`shmspto`**. Treasurer Vercel auto-deploys. Run **`node scripts/check-prod-deploy.mjs`**. Agents do not `vercel deploy` Stone Hill locally.

Staff-only exception: push `shmspto` `main` after Serena QA (no Rob wait), then run the check script.
5. **Default after a Stone Hill application ship:** also deploy Pavilion app code from the **same SHA** (`commons-pto-demo` and `commons-pto` as relevant). Almost every SHMS product change belongs on Pavilion too. **Hard rule:** Pavilion stays vanilla. No Stone Hill / SHMS branding, school PII, or SHMS-specific copy on Pavilion surfaces (demo gates + `vanillaizeIfDemo` / Commons surface still apply). Skip Pavilion only when the change is clearly SHMS-only (school CMS content, SHMS-only env, one-off school ops) or Rob says skip.
6. If the task is Pavilion-only (`commons-site`, demo vanillaize, trial packs), ship Pavilion projects only (same staging → OK → prod → push). Do not require a Stone Hill deploy.

Never put Stone Hill `DATABASE_URL` / Wix / Square env on Pavilion projects, or Pavilion `DATABASE_URL` / Stripe on Stone Hill.

At session start: `node scripts/commons-parity.mjs` is informational. Do not force catch-up unless Rob wants Pavilion on that SHA or the task is Pavilion-facing.

Plaid stays on the **Trial** account until paying Pavilion clients.

Vanillaize / demo gates still apply on Commons demo. After a Pavilion-facing ship, run `node scripts/commons-surface-check.mjs`.
